  "body": "> @topoldo would this work for you?\n\nI think this solution is OK because it is more flexible.\nIn the _description_ of the script (for example in a _readme.txt_ file) or in a _comment_ inside the script itself, you can warn potential user that, depending on the ART main program location, one should decide if (s)he wants to configure the non-standard path both for ART. IMHO this should work also for SMART, including the possibility of an installation of SMART in a location different from %APPDATALOCAL%, for example in C:\\Program Files\\SMART.\n\nRegards,\nTopoldo\n",
